    "proof": "Child cylinders refine the parent cylinder, so r_(wa)=r_w+k_a M_w with 0<=k_a<2^a. The integer r_w has one actual next valuation a*=v_2(3T^H(r_w)+1), hence realizes wa* and, because r_w is already below the child modulus, is its least representative. If another a had k_a=0, the same integer would have two different exact 2-adic valuations, impossible. The density bound is immediate. Stabilization means consecutive representatives are equal, so each later edge is the unique zero-lift edge.",
